🇺🇸🇸🇦 Why Would Saudi Arabia Call Trump? The US Puppet Show Continues

▪️Just like supposed "splits" with Europe or Canada followed by both governments obediently doubling down on US geopolitical objectives around the globe at their own expense, Saudi Arabia has long since been captured by and integrated as an extension of US foreign policy in West Asia and beyond and is using theatrics to sell rising costs because of this to the public;

▪️Why would Saudi Arabia "contact" the US president on military matters when the US is already running Saudi Arabia's military by proxy to begin with?

▪️The "Saudi" war on Ansarallah in Yemen has been conducted for YEARS by Saudi pilots using US warplanes maintained by US maintenance crews, using US munitions, guided to target using US ISR, gathered by US assets including US special operations forces on the ground inside Yemen - it is and has been a US war in all but name;

▪️So no, Saudi Arabia isn't contacting the US and asking for help, this is part of the puppet show put on for public perception management across the region, justifying greater spending on military, greater sacrifices by ordinary people across Saudi society, just like in Europe and Canada, for US interests - not their own;

▪️Reading local Saudi media, Ansarallah is being depicted just like Russia is in Europe as an "existential threat" that requires emergency action/sacrifice to confront - which translates into sacrificing for US interests at Saudi Arabia's expense;

▪️The client regime the US maintains in power in Riyadh will go along with it, the theater is to get everyone else to go along as well;
